ted_at":"2026-10-16T07:54:20.978-05:00","title":"Mull: note-taking with a language server / vscode extension","url":"https://github.com/stepchowfun/mull","score":12,"flags":0,"comment_count":8,"description":"\u003cp\u003eI've been writing notes as plain text files since forever, and it occurred to me that note-taking could benefit from the typical features that a language server provides: clickable links, autocomplete, hover previews, formatting, diagnostics, refactoring, etc. So I built a little language server and a vscode extension which adds syntax highlighting. Note-taking now feels more like writing code, and I get to use my favorite vscode keybindings (vim). Feedback is welcome!\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"I've been writing notes as plain text files since forever, and it occurred to me that note-taking could benefit from the typical features that a language server provides: clickable links, autocomplete, hover previews, formatting, diagnostics, refactoring, etc. So I built a little language server and a vscode extension which adds syntax highlighting. Note-taking now feels more like writing code, and I get to use my favorite vscode keybindings (vim). Feedback is welcome!","submitter_user":"lettuce","user_is_author":true,"tags":["editors"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xcacrh","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xcacrh/mull_note_taking_with_language_server"},{"short_id":"gtev9y","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:39:23.630-05:00","title":"Lessons learned building Fronteira, an MCP proxy with behavioral guardrails","url":"https://wiki.alcidesfonseca.com/blog/lessons-learned-building-fronteira/","score":-2,"flags":3,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"alcides","user_is_author":true,"tags":["security","vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/gtev9y","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/gtev9y/lessons_learned_building_fronteira_mcp"}]